==================== C. L95 ====================
  C1 static medium frame (medium unperturbed): p_chi = 0;  A = d^2L/d(chi_dot)^2 = 0
  C1 FRW: p_chi = -3*h*dlam(x0, x)*exp(3*h*x0);  A = 0;  d^2L/d(lam_dot)^2 = 0
  C2 FRW Hamiltonian: p_chi + 3 h a^3 dlam = 0 and p_lam = 0 are second class for h != 0 (bracket 3 h a^3); eliminating dlam leaves
     one canonical pair (dchi, p_chi) with H LINEAR in p_chi (A = 0): a first-order (parabolic) pair, unbounded in p_chi.
     At h = 0 the bracket vanishes: p_chi ~ 0 and p_lam ~ 0 are constraints and the pair carries no degree of freedom.
     L95's obstruction A A'/2 = 0 identically on both backgrounds.
